facts: The read-only values about a host.

Facts are a fixed set. Expressions read them as facts.os.id, and
templates as {{ .facts.os.id }}. A read of an unknown fact is an
error. winch reads the facts once per host per run, before the first
step, and again after a reboot. They describe the host before the run.

```yaml
# winch.yaml
name: demo
hosts:
  web1.example.com: {}
steps:
  - recipe: base
recipes:
  base:
    require:
      - !expr facts.os.id == "debian" and facts.os.version == "13"
    steps:
      - reboot:
          if_required: true
        when: !expr facts.reboot_required
```

Keys:
  os               map      -  The OS of the host.
  os.id            string   -  The ID of the OS, such as debian or ubuntu.
  os.version       string   -  The version of the release, such as 13 or 24.04.
  os.codename      string   -  The code name of the release, such as trixie or noble.
  os.arch          string   -  The architecture of the host, amd64 or arm64.
  reboot_required  boolean  -  true when the host waits for a reboot: /run/reboot-required exists, or a kernel in /boot is newer than the running kernel.

Run "winch doc facts.<key>" for the full text of a key.
